# Optional overlay for `pnpm local:up`, applied on top of the committed
# `e2e/stack.env`. Copy to `local.env` (gitignored) and edit. An EMPTY value
# unsets the variable inherited from `e2e/stack.env`.
#
# ── Real Google ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Connect a real Google account and import real locations from this stack. The
# runner then drops every `provider-sandbox` endpoint pin and selects the
# approved Google endpoints (`production-fixed`).
#
# Prerequisites, once, in the Google Cloud project that already carries the
# Business Profile API allowlist (the same project as production):
#   1. APIs & Services → Credentials → an OAuth 2.0 Client ID of type
#      "Web application" (a new "RepKey local" client keeps production's client
#      untouched; reusing production's client works too).
#   2. Authorised redirect URIs → add exactly:
#        http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/auth/google/callback
#      (Google accepts loopback URIs over http for web clients.)
#   3. The Google account you connect must manage at least one Business Profile
#      location, and must be a test user if the consent screen is in Testing.
#
# Real API quota is consumed and real reviewer data lands in the local
# database; `pnpm local:down` deletes that volume.
#
# REPKEY_LOCAL_GOOGLE=real
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=000000000000-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx.apps.googleusercontent.com
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=GOCSPX-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
